  ('Computer Science', 'AQA', 'gcse', '3.4', 'Computer Systems', 'Draw the truth table for OR.', '0 OR 0 = 0; 0 OR 1 = 1; 1 OR 0 = 1; 1 OR 1 = 1.', 22),
  ('Computer Science', 'AQA', 'gcse', '3.4', 'Computer Systems', 'Draw the truth table for NOT.', 'NOT 0 = 1; NOT 1 = 0.', 23),
  ('Computer Science', 'AQA', 'gcse', '3.4', 'Computer Systems', 'What is a high-level language?', 'A programming language close to human language, e.g. Python or Java.', 24),
  ('Computer Science', 'AQA', 'gcse', '3.4', 'Computer Systems', 'What is a low-level language?', 'A language close to machine code, e.g. assembly language or machine code.', 25),
  ('Computer Science', 'AQA', 'gcse', '3.4', 'Computer Systems', 'Give an advantage of high-level languages.', 'They are easier to read, write and debug, and are portable between computers.', 26),
  ('Computer Science', 'AQA', 'gcse', '3.4', 'Computer Systems', 'Give an advantage of low-level languages.', 'They give direct control over hardware and can be more efficient in speed and memory.', 27),
  ('Computer Science', 'AQA', 'gcse', '3.4', 'Computer Systems', 'What is machine code?', 'Binary instructions that the CPU can execute directly.', 28),
  ('Computer Science', 'AQA', 'gcse', '3.4', 'Computer Systems', 'What is assembly language?', 'A low-level language that uses mnemonics (e.g. ADD, LDA) to represent machine code instructions.', 29),
  ('Computer Science', 'AQA', 'gcse', '3.4', 'Computer Systems', 'What is a translator?', 'A program that converts source code into machine code.', 30),
  ('Computer Science', 'AQA', 'gcse', '3.5', 'Fundamentals of Computer Networks', 'What is a network?', 'Two or more computers connected together to share data and resources.', 1),
  ('Computer Science', 'AQA', 'gcse', '3.5', 'Fundamentals of Computer Networks', 'What is a LAN?', 'A local area network covering a small geographical area, such as a school, using its own hardware.', 2),
  ('Computer Science', 'AQA', 'gcse', '3.5', 'Fundamentals of Computer Networks', 'What is a WAN?', 'A wide area network covering a large geographical area, often using third-party infrastructure; the internet is the largest WAN.', 3),
  ('Computer Science', 'AQA', 'gcse', '3.5', 'Fundamentals of Computer Networks', 'What factors affect network performance?', 'Bandwidth, number of users, transmission media, errors, and interference.', 4),
  ('Computer Science', 'AQA', 'gcse', '3.5', 'Fundamentals of Computer Networks', 'What is bandwidth?', 'The amount of data that can be transmitted per second.', 5),
  ('Computer Science', 'AQA', 'gcse', '3.5', 'Fundamentals of Computer Networks', 'What is a client–server network?', 'A network where servers provide services and resources to client computers.', 6),
  ('Computer Science', 'AQA', 'gcse', '3.5', 'Fundamentals of Computer Networks', 'What is a peer-to-peer network?', 'A network where all computers have equal status and share resources directly with each other.', 7),
  ('Computer Science', 'AQA', 'gcse', '3.5', 'Fundamentals of Computer Networks', 'Give an advantage of a client–server network.', 'Centralised security, backups and file management.', 8),
  ('Computer Science', 'AQA', 'gcse', '3.5', 'Fundamentals of Computer Networks', 'Give an advantage of a peer-to-peer network.', 'Cheap and easy to set up, with no dependence on a server.', 9),
  ('Computer Science', 'AQA', 'gcse', '3.5', 'Fundamentals of Computer Networks', 'What is a wireless access point (WAP)?', 'A device that allows wireless devices to connect to a wired network.', 10),
  ('Computer Science', 'AQA', 'gcse', '3.5', 'Fundamentals of Computer Networks', 'What is a router?', 'A device that forwards data packets between networks, e.g. between a LAN and the internet.', 11),
  ('Computer Science', 'AQA', 'gcse', '3.5', 'Fundamentals of Computer Networks', 'What is a switch?', 'A device that connects devices on a LAN and sends data only to the intended device using MAC addresses.', 12),
  ('Computer Science', 'AQA', 'gcse', '3.5', 'Fundamentals of Computer Networks', 'What is a NIC?', 'A network interface card (controller), which allows a device to connect to a network.', 13),
  ('Computer Science', 'AQA', 'gcse', '3.5', 'Fundamentals of Computer Networks', 'What is the internet?', 'A worldwide collection of interconnected networks.', 14),
  ('Computer Science', 'AQA', 'gcse', '3.5', 'Fundamentals of Computer Networks', 'What is DNS?', 'The Domain Name System, which translates domain names (e.g. bbc.co.uk) into IP addresses.', 15),
  ('Computer Science', 'AQA', 'gcse', '3.5', 'Fundamentals of Computer Networks', 'What is hosting?', 'Storing websites or files on a server connected to the internet so others can access them.', 16),
  ('Computer Science', 'AQA', 'gcse', '3.5', 'Fundamentals of Computer Networks', 'What is the cloud?', 'Remote servers accessed over the internet to store data and run software.', 17),
  ('Computer Science', 'AQA', 'gcse', '3.5', 'Fundamentals of Computer Networks', 'Give an advantage and disadvantage of the cloud.', 'Advantage: access from anywhere, no need for local storage. Disadvantage: needs internet access and raises security concerns.', 18),
  ('Computer Science', 'AQA', 'gcse', '3.5', 'Fundamentals of Computer Networks', 'What is a star topology?', 'All devices connect to a central switch.', 19),
  ('Computer Science', 'AQA', 'gcse', '3.5', 'Fundamentals of Computer Networks', 'What is a mesh topology?', 'Devices are connected to many other devices, so data has several possible routes.', 20),
  ('Computer Science', 'AQA', 'gcse', '3.5', 'Fundamentals of Computer Networks', 'Give an advantage of a star topology.', 'If one cable fails, the other devices are unaffected, and it is easy to add devices.', 21),
  ('Computer Science', 'AQA', 'gcse', '3.5', 'Fundamentals of Computer Networks', 'Give an advantage of a mesh topology.', 'No single point of failure; data can take another route if a connection fails.', 22),
  ('Computer Science', 'AQA', 'gcse', '3.5', 'Fundamentals of Computer Networks', 'What is Wi-Fi?', 'A wireless networking standard using radio waves to connect devices to a network.', 23),
  ('Computer Science', 'AQA', 'gcse', '3.5', 'Fundamentals of Computer Networks', 'What is Ethernet?', 'A wired networking standard for connecting devices in a LAN.', 24),
  ('Computer Science', 'AQA', 'gcse', '3.5', 'Fundamentals of Computer Networks', 'What is an IP address?', 'A unique address given to each device on a network, used to route data.', 25),
  ('Computer Science', 'AQA', 'gcse', '3.5', 'Fundamentals of Computer Networks', 'What is a MAC address?', 'A unique, permanent hardware address assigned to a network interface.', 26),
  ('Computer Science', 'AQA', 'gcse', '3.5', 'Fundamentals of Computer Networks', 'What is a protocol?', 'A set of rules for how data is transmitted across a network.', 27),
  ('Computer Science', 'AQA', 'gcse', '3.5', 'Fundamentals of Computer Networks', 'What are TCP/IP and HTTP used for?', 'TCP/IP: sending data across the internet in packets. HTTP: requesting and transferring web pages.', 28),
  ('Computer Science', 'AQA', 'gcse', '3.5', 'Fundamentals of Computer Networks', 'What is HTTPS?', 'A secure version of HTTP that encrypts data between browser and server.', 29),
  ('Computer Science', 'AQA', 'gcse', '3.5', 'Fundamentals of Computer Networks', 'What is the concept of layers in networking?', 'Protocols are divided into layers, each handling a specific part of communication, making development and troubleshooting easier.', 30),
  ('Computer Science', 'AQA', 'gcse', '3.6', 'Cyber Security', 'What is malware?', 'Malicious software designed to damage, disrupt or gain unauthorised access to computer systems.', 1),
  ('Computer Science', 'AQA', 'gcse', '3.6', 'Cyber Security', 'What is a virus?', 'Malware that attaches itself to files and spreads when those files are copied or opened.', 2),
  ('Computer Science', 'AQA', 'gcse', '3.6', 'Cyber Security', 'What is a worm?', 'Malware that replicates itself and spreads across networks without user action.', 3),
  ('Computer Science', 'AQA', 'gcse', '3.6', 'Cyber Security', 'What is a Trojan?', 'Malware disguised as legitimate software.', 4),
  ('Computer Science', 'AQA', 'gcse', '3.6', 'Cyber Security', 'What is ransomware?', 'Malware that encrypts a user''s files and demands payment for their release.', 5),
  ('Computer Science', 'AQA', 'gcse', '3.6', 'Cyber Security', 'What is spyware?', 'Malware that secretly monitors user activity and collects information.', 6),
  ('Computer Science', 'AQA', 'gcse', '3.6', 'Cyber Security', 'What is social engineering?', 'Manipulating people into giving away confidential information.', 7),
  ('Computer Science', 'AQA', 'gcse', '3.6', 'Cyber Security', 'What is phishing?', 'Sending fake emails or messages that appear to be from a trusted source to trick people into revealing personal information.', 8),
  ('Computer Science', 'AQA', 'gcse', '3.6', 'Cyber Security', 'What is shouldering?', 'Watching someone enter a password or PIN over their shoulder.', 9),
  ('Computer Science', 'AQA', 'gcse', '3.6', 'Cyber Security', 'What is a brute-force attack?', 'Trying every possible combination of characters to guess a password.', 10),
  ('Computer Science', 'AQA', 'gcse', '3.6', 'Cyber Security', 'What is a denial of service (DoS) attack?', 'Flooding a server with requests so it can''t respond to genuine users.', 11),
  ('Computer Science', 'AQA', 'gcse', '3.6', 'Cyber Security', 'What is data interception?', 'Capturing data as it travels across a network, e.g. using packet sniffers.', 12),
  ('Computer Science', 'AQA', 'gcse', '3.6', 'Cyber Security', 'What is SQL injection?', 'Entering malicious SQL code into an input field to access or change a database.', 13),
  ('Computer Science', 'AQA', 'gcse', '3.6', 'Cyber Security', 'What is penetration testing?', 'Authorised simulated attacks on a system to find vulnerabilities.', 14),
  ('Computer Science', 'AQA', 'gcse', '3.6', 'Cyber Security', 'What is anti-malware software?', 'Software that detects, prevents and removes malware.', 15),
  ('Computer Science', 'AQA', 'gcse', '3.6', 'Cyber Security', 'What is a firewall?', 'Hardware or software that monitors network traffic and blocks unauthorised access.', 16),
  ('Computer Science', 'AQA', 'gcse', '3.6', 'Cyber Security', 'What are user access levels?', 'Permissions that control which files and resources different users can access.', 17),
  ('Computer Science', 'AQA', 'gcse', '3.6', 'Cyber Security', 'Why are strong passwords important?', 'They are harder to guess or brute-force, protecting accounts from unauthorised access.', 18),
  ('Computer Science', 'AQA', 'gcse', '3.6', 'Cyber Security', 'What makes a strong password?', 'A long password mixing upper and lower case letters, numbers and symbols, not based on personal information.', 19),
  ('Computer Science', 'AQA', 'gcse', '3.6', 'Cyber Security', 'What is encryption?', 'Scrambling data using a key so it can only be read by someone with the correct key.', 20),
  ('Computer Science', 'AQA', 'gcse', '3.6', 'Cyber Security', 'What is physical security?', 'Protecting hardware from theft or damage, e.g. locks, CCTV and security guards.', 21),
  ('Computer Science', 'AQA', 'gcse', '3.6', 'Cyber Security', 'What is two-factor authentication?', 'Requiring two forms of verification, such as a password and a code sent to a phone.', 22),
  ('Computer Science', 'AQA', 'gcse', '3.6', 'Cyber Security', 'How can SQL injection be prevented?', 'Validating input and using parameterised queries.', 23),
  ('Computer Science', 'AQA', 'gcse', '3.6', 'Cyber Security', 'How can phishing be prevented?', 'User training, spam filters, and checking email addresses and links before clicking.', 24),
  ('Computer Science', 'AQA', 'gcse', '3.6', 'Cyber Security', 'How can brute-force attacks be prevented?', 'Strong passwords, account lockouts after failed attempts, and CAPTCHAs.', 25),
  ('Computer Science', 'AQA', 'gcse', '3.6', 'Cyber Security', 'How can DoS attacks be reduced?', 'Firewalls, traffic filtering, and increasing server capacity.', 26),
  ('Computer Science', 'AQA', 'gcse', '3.6', 'Cyber Security', 'What is a vulnerability?', 'A weakness in a system that can be exploited by an attacker.', 27),
  ('Computer Science', 'AQA', 'gcse', '3.6', 'Cyber Security', 'Why do organisations need network policies?', 'To define acceptable use, security procedures and responsibilities, reducing risks.', 28),
  ('Computer Science', 'AQA', 'gcse', '3.6', 'Cyber Security', 'What is a backup?', 'A copy of data stored separately so it can be restored if the original is lost or damaged.', 29),
  ('Computer Science', 'AQA', 'gcse', '3.6', 'Cyber Security', 'What is the difference between hackers and malware?', 'Hackers are people who gain unauthorised access; malware is software used to cause harm.', 30),
  ('Computer Science', 'AQA', 'gcse', '3.7', 'Relational Databases and SQL', 'What is a database?', 'An organised, structured collection of data that can be easily searched and managed.', 1),
  ('Computer Science', 'AQA', 'gcse', '3.7', 'Relational Databases and SQL', 'What is a relational database?', 'A database that stores data in linked tables to reduce data redundancy.', 2),
  ('Computer Science', 'AQA', 'gcse', '3.7', 'Relational Databases and SQL', 'What is a table?', 'A collection of records about one type of entity, e.g. Students.', 3),
  ('Computer Science', 'AQA', 'gcse', '3.7', 'Relational Databases and SQL', 'What is a record?', 'A row in a table, containing data about one item.', 4),
  ('Computer Science', 'AQA', 'gcse', '3.7', 'Relational Databases and SQL', 'What is a field?', 'A column in a table, containing one piece of data about each record.', 5),
  ('Computer Science', 'AQA', 'gcse', '3.7', 'Relational Databases and SQL', 'What is a primary key?', 'A field that uniquely identifies each record in a table.', 6),
  ('Computer Science', 'AQA', 'gcse', '3.7', 'Relational Databases and SQL', 'What is a foreign key?', 'A field in one table that is the primary key in another table, used to link them.', 7),
  ('Computer Science', 'AQA', 'gcse', '3.7', 'Relational Databases and SQL', 'What is data redundancy?', 'Unnecessary duplication of data.', 8),
  ('Computer Science', 'AQA', 'gcse', '3.7', 'Relational Databases and SQL', 'What is data inconsistency?', 'When the same data has different values in different places.', 9),
  ('Computer Science', 'AQA', 'gcse', '3.7', 'Relational Databases and SQL', 'How do relational databases reduce redundancy?', 'Data is stored once in separate linked tables, rather than repeated.', 10),
  ('Computer Science', 'AQA', 'gcse', '3.7', 'Relational Databases and SQL', 'What does SELECT do in SQL?', 'Retrieves specified fields from a table.', 11),
  ('Computer Science', 'AQA', 'gcse', '3.7', 'Relational Databases and SQL', 'What does FROM do in SQL?', 'Specifies which table(s) to retrieve data from.', 12),
  ('Computer Science', 'AQA', 'gcse', '3.7', 'Relational Databases and SQL', 'What does WHERE do in SQL?', 'Filters records based on a condition.', 13),
  ('Computer Science', 'AQA', 'gcse', '3.7', 'Relational Databases and SQL', 'What does ORDER BY do in SQL?', 'Sorts the results in ascending (ASC) or descending (DESC) order.', 14),
  ('Computer Science', 'AQA', 'gcse', '3.7', 'Relational Databases and SQL', 'Write SQL to select the name and age of students older than 15.', 'SELECT Name, Age FROM Students WHERE Age > 15;', 15),
  ('Computer Science', 'AQA', 'gcse', '3.7', 'Relational Databases and SQL', 'Write SQL to select all fields from Products ordered by price, highest first.', 'SELECT * FROM Products ORDER BY Price DESC;', 16),
  ('Computer Science', 'AQA', 'gcse', '3.7', 'Relational Databases and SQL', 'What does * mean in SQL?', 'All fields.', 17),
  ('Computer Science', 'AQA', 'gcse', '3.7', 'Relational Databases and SQL', 'What does INSERT INTO do in SQL?', 'Adds a new record to a table.', 18),
  ('Computer Science', 'AQA', 'gcse', '3.7', 'Relational Databases and SQL', 'Write SQL to add a student called Ali, aged 16.', 'INSERT INTO Students (Name, Age) VALUES (''Ali'', 16);', 19),
